---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  GradientBannerPlayground,
  GradientBannerVariants,
  GradientBannerSizes,
  GradientBannerSizesInContext,
  GradientBannerPanels,
  GradientBannerProgressStates,
  GradientBannerPrompts,
  GradientBannerAgentActivity,
  GradientBannerArtOnly,
} from "../../components/GradientBannerDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Gradient Banner"
  description="Decorative gradient art with readable panels, badges, and progress on top."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Gradient Banner</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Soft gradient art for prompt cards, onboarding, and showcase panels. Put
    text on a panel so it stays readable on every color.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><GradientBannerPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Gradient banner usage"
      code={`import {
  GradientBanner,
  GradientBannerBadge,
  GradientBannerPanel,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/gradient-banner";

<GradientBanner variant="iris" size="md">
  <GradientBannerPanel tone="dark">
    <GradientBannerBadge>Example</GradientBannerBadge>
    <span>How agents work in TulipFarm</span>
  </GradientBannerPanel>
</GradientBanner>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> picks the colors and defaults to <code>"aurora"</code
      >. <code>size</code> sets the minimum height, padding, and corner radius: <code
        >sm</code
      > 96px, <code>md</code> 160px, <code>lg</code> 240px (default), and <code
        >xl</code
      > 360px. Children sit centered on the art; a banner without children draws only
      the art.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants</h2>
    <p>
      Six color stories. Text placed straight on <code>cobalt</code> turns pearl so
      it stays readable on deep blue; the other variants use dark ink.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerVariants client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes and texture</h2>
    <p>
      A film grain sits over the art by default. Set <code
        >texture=&#123;false&#125;</code
      > for flat color, for example when many banners share a screen.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerSizes client:load />
    <p>Each size with the content it is made for:</p>
    <GradientBannerSizesInContext client:load />
    <GradientBannerArtOnly client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Panels and badges</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Prompt card"
      code={`<GradientBanner variant="lagoon" size="md">
  <GradientBannerPanel>
    <BrandIcon brand="slack" size="glyph" />
    <span>Post the weekly update in #team</span>
  </GradientBannerPanel>
</GradientBanner>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>GradientBannerPanel</code> is a solid <code>"light"</code> (default) or
      <code>"dark"</code> surface. Badges and progress inside a dark panel switch
      to dark fills on their own. Long words wrap instead of overflowing.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerPanels client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Progress</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Progress"
      code={`<GradientBannerProgress value={percent} aria-label="Spring launch email progress" />`}
    />
    <p>
      A 4px <code>progressbar</code> in the current text color. <code
        >value</code
      > is a percent; values outside 0–100 are clamped. Give it a name with <code
        >aria-label</code
      >.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerProgressStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Prompt carousel</h2>
    <p>
      An integration sheet suggests things to ask. Each card rotates through the
      variants from a stable start per app, so the same app always gets the same
      colors. The row scrolls sideways and snaps; focus it and use the arrow
      keys.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerPrompts client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Showcase</h2>
    <p>
      The sign-in page fills half the screen with an <code>xl</code> banner that plays
      scripted agent runs: a dark example label, a panel with avatar, badge, progress,
      and steps, then a result badge. It starts paused when reduced motion is on;
      Pause stops it at any time.
    </p>
    <GradientBannerAgentActivity client:load />
    <p>
      Agent runs, app prompts, and timing in these examples are sample code. The
      package only draws the banner, panels, badges, and progress.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The art and its texture are <code>aria-hidden</code>; only children are
      announced. Banners are not interactive, so focus goes to the controls you
      put inside. Progress has <code>role="progressbar"</code> with rounded <code
        >aria-valuenow</code
      >. Its fill eases over 180ms; reduced motion turns that off.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
